id: drunken-fist-power-of-the-bottle
name: Power of the Bottle
order: 1
slot: trait
# Its [Constant] effects: a [Triggered] one that may be used outside the Transformation (the user's).
constant: 1
resource: toppling
resourceLabel: Toppling
resourceMax: 3
description: >
  Whether through imitation or through actually imbibing, your movement is like that of a drunkard, but with combat skills woven in.
text: >
  Power of the Bottle: Whether through imitation or through actually imbibing, your movement is like that of a drunkard, but with combat skills woven in.
  (1)-[Constant]: If you drink from a Sake Bottle, instead of entering the Drunk State, you may use the Transformation Maneuver to enter this Transformation as an Out-of-Sequence Maneuver.
  (2)-[Passive]: The first effect of the Tipsy Level of the Drunk Special State increases your Saving Throws and Combat Rolls instead of reducing them.
  (3)-[Triggered, Resource]: If you successfully dodge an Opponent's Attacking Maneuver, gain a stack of Toppling (max. 3).
  (4)-[Triggered]: If you target an Opponent with an Attacking Maneuver, you may spend any number of Toppling stacks to increase the Strike and Wound Rolls of that Attacking Maneuver by 1(T) for each Toppling stack spent.

---

# (1) Constant: from a Sake Bottle, this instead of the Drunk State - the Transformation Maneuver out of sequence, the table's to offer.
# (2) The Drunk State's 1st effect raising your Saving Throws and Combat Rolls instead of lowering them.
[passive, effect 2]
if (inState("drunk")) {
    save.all += 2 * states.drunk * 1(T);
    combatRolls += 2 * states.drunk * 1(T);
}

# (3) An Opponent's Attacking Maneuver dodged: a stack of Toppling (max. 3).
[triggered/dodged-attack, effect 3]
toppling.stacks += 1;

# (4) Spent on an attack: Strike and Wound 1(T) a stack - asked at its Strike (chat.mjs stacksOnRoll).
[passive, effect 4]
allow stacksOnRoll.toppling;
